# Line endings.
#
# Some files here are compared byte for byte -- the generated phoneme-bank
# bundle against its generator's output, and (from stage 0 of the C rewrite)
# golden corpora against a fresh render. Git rewriting line endings on checkout
# breaks that comparison: on Windows with core.autocrlf=true the working tree
# gets CRLF where the generator writes LF, and the file looks changed when its
# content is identical. That already happened once -- see docs/ROADMAP.md,
# phase 2 prerequisites.
#
# The rule: anything compared byte for byte is pinned to LF, and anything
# binary is never converted at all. The last matching pattern wins.

# Default: let git decide what is text, and keep LF in the repository.
* text=auto

# Generated. tools/build-banks.js writes LF and its --check mode compares
# against what is on disk.
src/engine/banks/bundled.js text eol=lf

# Golden corpora and their manifests. Byte-for-byte comparison is the whole
# point of these, so they must arrive exactly as they were captured.
goldens/** text eol=lf

# C sources and the build, pinned so three compilers on two operating systems
# are reading identical bytes.
*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf

# Shell scripts break if they arrive with CRLF.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Never convert. Listed last so these win over every rule above, including
# goldens/** for a captured WAV.
*.wav  binary
*.bin  binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.nvda-addon binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp3  binary
